### ============================================================
### Spring Security Reference - REST Client Testing File
### ============================================================
### Use with VS Code REST Client extension or IntelliJ HTTP Client
###
### HOW TO USE:
### 1. Start the app: mvn spring-boot:run -pl rest-api
### 2. Run "Login as Admin" request below
### 3. Copy the token from response
### 4. Replace @jwtToken value with your token
### 5. Run other requests!
### ============================================================

### Variables - UPDATE THESE!
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@jwtToken = PASTE_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================================
### 🏥 STEP 1: Health Check (Run First!)
### ============================================================

### Check if app is running
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/public/hello

### Health endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### ============================================================
### 🔑 STEP 2: JWT Authentication
### ============================================================

### 2a. Login as ADMIN - Copy the "token" from response!
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=admin&password=password

### 2b. Login as USER - Copy the "token" from response!
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

username=user&password=password

### ============================================================
### 🔑 STEP 3: Use JWT Token (Update @jwtToken above first!)
### ============================================================

### Check who you are
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/info
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### Access admin endpoint (needs ROLE_ADMIN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/secure
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### Access user endpoint (needs ROLE_USER or ROLE_ADMIN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/secure
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### ============================================================
### 🗄️ JDBC Authentication (Database Users)
### ============================================================
### Credentials: jdbcadmin/password, jdbcuser/password
### Base64: echo -n "jdbcadmin:password" | base64

### JDBC Admin - View users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jdbc/users
Authorization: Basic amRiY2FkbWluOnBhc3N3b3Jk

### JDBC User - View users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jdbc/users
Authorization: Basic amRiY3VzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=

### JDBC Admin - Access admin endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/secure
Authorization: Basic amRiY2FkbWluOnBhc3N3b3Jk

### JDBC User - Access user endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/secure
Authorization: Basic amRiY3VzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=

### JDBC User - Try admin endpoint (should fail with 403!)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/secure
Authorization: Basic amRiY3VzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=

### ============================================================
### 🏢 LDAP Authentication (Directory Users)
### ============================================================
### ⚠️ LDAP server disabled by default!
### Enable with: --spring.ldap.embedded.enabled=true
### Credentials: ldapadmin/password, ldapuser/password

### LDAP Admin - View users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ldap/users
Authorization: Basic bGRhcGFkbWluOnBhc3N3b3Jk

### LDAP User - View users
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ldap/users
Authorization: Basic bGRhcHVzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=

### LDAP Admin - Access admin endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/secure
Authorization: Basic bGRhcGFkbWluOnBhc3N3b3Jk

### LDAP User - Access user endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/secure
Authorization: Basic bGRhcHVzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=

### ============================================================
### 🌐 OAuth2 Social Login (Browser Required)
### ============================================================
### Open these URLs in your BROWSER, not here!

### Google OAuth2 Login (open in browser)
# http://localhost:8080/oauth2/authorization/google

### GitHub OAuth2 Login (open in browser)
# http://localhost:8080/oauth2/authorization/github

### OAuth2 User Profile (after browser login)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/oauth2/profile

### ============================================================
### 🧪 Error Testing
### ============================================================

### Invalid JWT Token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/user/secure
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token-12345

### Missing Auth Header (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/secure

### Invalid Basic Auth Credentials (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jdbc/users
Authorization: Basic aW52YWxpZDppbnZhbGlk

### Wrong Role - User accessing Admin (expect 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/secure
Authorization: Basic amRiY3VzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=

### ============================================================
### 📋 Quick Reference
### ============================================================
###
### JWT Users:
###   admin / password  → ROLE_ADMIN
###   user / password   → ROLE_USER
###
### JDBC Users (Base64 encoded):
###   jdbcadmin:password → amRiY2FkbWluOnBhc3N3b3Jk
###   jdbcuser:password  → amRiY3VzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=
###
### LDAP Users (Base64 encoded):
###   ldapadmin:password → bGRhcGFkbWluOnBhc3N3b3Jk
###   ldapuser:password  → bGRhcHVzZXI6cGFzc3dvcmQ=
###
### To encode credentials yourself:
###   echo -n "username:password" | base64
### ============================================================
